8214	{"artifactId":"LLD-72b1bee074ba2dab-s1","entry":{"id":"migrated-LLD-72b1bee074ba2dab-s1-review","actor":{"id":"insrc:daemon","kind":"agent","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-19T04:05:41.972Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"review: block","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"block","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The proposed lookup and adoption linking address the recorded S4-1 outcome.","evidence":"S4-1 explicitly requests 'link adopted Story and Task issues in ensureUnitIssueDetailed'. The actual adoption branch records and returns the issue without linking; the proposed change targets that branch. Analyzer tools were unavailable, so verification used source and artifact reads. [files: docs/plans/s4-open-issues.md, src/workflow/tracker/unit-issue.ts]","action":"Preserve this focused scope.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Label adoption currently skips linking, whereas successful creation records failed links for retry.","evidence":"The adoption branch executes 'recordUnit(unit, adopted, now())' and immediately returns. The creation branch calls linkSubIssue and stores '{ parent: parentRef, childId: created.value.id }' on failure. The local-resolution branch invokes retryPendingLink. [files: src/workflow/tracker/unit-issue.ts]","action":"Retain the existing creation and local-resolution behavior.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The ref-to-id operation is new, and the existing linking operation consumes a numeric database id through the injectable gh runner.","evidence":"IssueOps has no resolveIssueId member. ghLinkSubIssue takes 'childId: number' and calls runGh with '-F', 'sub_issue_id=${childId}'. runGh uses the _exec seam configured by _setTrackerExecForTests. [files: src/workflow/tracker/port.ts, src/workflow/tracker/github.ts, src/workflow/tracker/github-adapter.ts]","action":"Implement the new lookup through the stated runner and adapter.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"Recording adoption first can be followed by saving its failed link through the existing recordUnit behavior.","evidence":"recordUnit selects 'prior !== undefined && prior.issue === issue ? prior : ...'. After the initial adoption write, another recordUnit call for that issue ignores a supplied pendingLink. The design specifies linking 'after recordUnit' but does not specify changing this preservation rule or explicitly patching the record. Such reuse loses the retry marker, and subsequent local ensures skip linking. [files: src/workflow/tracker/unit-issue.ts, src/workflow/tracker/refs.ts]","action":"Specify an explicit pendingLink patch that preserves revision and extras, or change recordUnit's merge semantics. Test persistence after the initial adoption record already exists.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Existing parent-and-childId records remain readable without a data rewrite.","evidence":"UnitIssue currently stores '{ readonly parent: string; readonly childId: number }'. readTrackerMeta reads the JSON without transforming this field, and retryPendingLink links directly using pending.childId. Retaining that branch supports existing records. [files: src/workflow/tracker/refs.ts, src/workflow/tracker/unit-issue.ts]","action":"Keep the childId-first retry branch and the proposed legacy-record test.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.2","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"HIGH","premise":"The storage change is rollbackable after child-only records have been written.","evidence":"The old retry implementation unconditionally calls 'port.issueOps.linkSubIssue(pending.parent, pending.childId)'. A new '{ parent, child }' record supplies undefined after rollback; ghLinkSubIssue then submits 'sub_issue_id=undefined'. Forward compatibility with old records does not establish rollback compatibility. [files: src/workflow/tracker/unit-issue.ts, src/workflow/tracker/github.ts]","action":"State that rollback requires resolving or converting child-only records, or introduce a compatible reader before allowing those writes.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"boundaries.1","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"There are no HLD shared contracts or other Story ownership constraints to honor.","evidence":"AMD-315d510cb28100e2-11 declares 'type': 'sharedContract.methodAdd', 'contractId': 'sc1', and 'status': 'pending'. Its purpose says 'the GitHub adapter test is s1’s to add'. S4-1 names the prerequisite 's1 to agree; then link adopted Story and Task issues'. Standalone metadata does not remove that existing shared-contract dependency. [files: .insrc/artifacts/AMD-315d510cb28100e2-11.json, docs/plans/s4-open-issues.md, .insrc/artifacts/LLD-72b1bee074ba2dab-s1.json]","action":"Document the sc1 dependency and resolve the pending amendment and ownership before treating the port addition as an agreed contract.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"The existing ref parser rejects every ref that is not owner/repo#N.","evidence":"parseIssueRef checks only the positions of '#' and '/'; it returns the remaining number string without validation. Values such as 'o/r#abc' and '/#' pass. github-adapter.ts explicitly notes: 'parseIssueRef alone only checks the separators' and uses a separate regex for assignee operations. [files: src/workflow/tracker/refs.ts, src/workflow/tracker/github-adapter.ts]","action":"Specify strict validation for ghGetIssueId and test malformed number and empty owner/repo components.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"error-paths.2","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"Using runGh and attempt yields only rejected or unreachable lookup failures.","evidence":"classifyGhFailure also returns 'missing-tool' for ENOENT and 'missing-signin' for authentication failures. The adapter's failure function preserves GhCommandError.kind. Thus the proposed implementation exposes more failure kinds than section 2.1 declares. [files: src/workflow/tracker/github.ts, src/workflow/tracker/github-adapter.ts, src/workflow/tracker/port.ts]","action":"Declare all PortFailureKind outcomes and apply the pending-link behavior to each.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The ac1 mapping covers every upstream acceptance criterion.","evidence":"The standalone artifact and repository searches yielded this LLD but no corresponding upstream Story acceptance-criteria artifact. S4-1 supplies an outcome, and existing unit-issue tests provide commitThenFail and failed-link retry fixtures, but they cannot establish that the synthetic ac1 exhausts upstream criteria. [files: .insrc/artifacts/LLD-72b1bee074ba2dab-s1.json, docs/plans/s4-open-issues.md, src/workflow/tracker/__tests__/unit-issue.test.ts]","action":"Define explicit acceptance criteria for Story and Task adoption, lookup/link retries, Epic exclusion, and legacy pending records, then map each to a specific test.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"could-not-verify"}],"counts":{"high":2,"med":3,"low":5,"unverified":1},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-19T04:05:41.972Z","model":"cli-codex:gpt-6-astra","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
